---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Who I am and what this site is for."
	pubDate={new Date('August 28 2026')}
>
	<p>
		I'm Aiden Ferrante, a data science master's student. I write about where artificial
		intelligence is actually heading — the compute and capital behind it, what the systems can
		genuinely do, what that means for human work, and who ends up making the rules.
	</p>

	<p>
		There is a lot of commentary on all of this and most of it is written by people with no
		working relationship to the thing they are describing. My angle is that I build the systems I
		write about. I run open-weight models on my own hardware, keep a financial data lake I can
		query instead of recalling headlines, have a small robot on my desk that fails at things, and
		write agent loops from scratch to find out which parts of the frameworks are load-bearing.
		That doesn't make me right, but it does mean my opinions have somewhere to be wrong.
	</p>

	<p>
		The <a href="/projects">projects page</a> is the map of that work. I also make videos working
		through the technical material from first principles, and each one gets a written companion
		post here.
	</p>

	<p>
		If you're hiring, collaborating, or want to argue with something I wrote —
		<a href="mailto:ferranteaiden6@gmail.com">email me</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
